1. Data inconsistency between widgets
If multiple widgets use their own setState() to manage the user's playlist, one widget might show an updated playlist while another still displays old data.
This happens because each widget manages its own state independently.

2. Difficult maintenance and debugging
As the app grows, multiple widgets may contain duplicate playlist logic, such as adding or removing songs. This makes bugs harder to find and fix because a 
change in one widget may not be reflected in others.
